This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - Muhammad Arslan, the product owner, is directing a client-only React + TypeScript **Loan EMI Calculator** for a job take-home. I write the code; he reviews and approves at gates.
   - CLAUDE.md rules, which must keep applying:
     - money is never a JS `number` (decimal.js only);
     - the algorithm in spec §5.2 is used exactly;
     - all visible text comes from `src/ui/copy.ts` and matches spec §7 exactly;
     - inputs are `type="text"`;
     - no new dependencies beyond spec §2 without asking (the pre-approved tooling list is in §2);
     - no network at runtime;
     - tests are the contract: after Gate G3, don't edit tests or the freeze scope of §12.4; if a test seems wrong, stop and explain to the owner;
     - never weaken, skip or delete tests;
     - **never change a story's Status without the owner's explicit approval**;
     - **never edit docs/app-roles.md, docs/jobs-to-be-done.md or ACs**: propose changes, which the owner edits or approves;
     - layer boundaries (domain imports nothing from ui or storage; storage imports nothing from ui);
     - tests titled `[AC-x.y]`;
     - small conventional commits;
     - a gate summary at each phase;
     - honesty: never claim more than the command output shows;
     - **record every decision in docs/spec/decision-log.md, append-only (D-24; owner: "keep all decision logs")**;
     - import `Decimal` only from `src/domain/money.ts`.
   - Workflow: phases with gates, defined in loop-plan.md.
     - Done: Phase 1 (G1), Phase 2 (G2), Phase 3 (G3, plus G3b for the visuals) and Phase 4 (groups 1 to 6; G4.6 closed). The redesign change cycle and the visuals change cycle are implemented.
     - Remaining: the visuals mini-gate, Phase 5 (whole-app review and the owner's manual checklist on desktop and phone, then the owner decides Statuses) and Phase 6 (README, push to GitHub, Pages deploy, smoke tests).
   - Most recent owner requests:
     - **visuals:** all four charts approved (D-65);
     - **sticky form:** "can you also freeze the actual calculator on right, when you scroll the space on left is empty" (D-69);
     - the owner replied "ok" to my status updates.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **Stack:** Node 24.16.0 (Windows, Git Bash plus PowerShell). Exact pinned versions:
     - React 19.3.1, TypeScript 6.0.3, Vite 8.3.4, Vitest 5.0.5, jsdom 30.1.3;
     - Playwright 1.64.1 (chromium, firefox, webkit), fast-check 4.10.2, decimal.js 10.6.0 (configured clone: precision 40, ROUND_HALF_UP);
     - ESLint 9.39.5 with typescript-eslint, react-hooks and jsx-a11y; Prettier 3.9.10.
   - **`npm run verify`** = lint → format:check → typecheck → test → build → size (< 150 KB gzipped) → test:e2e → `trace --results`.
     - **Always run Playwright with `CI=1`**, because a stale preview server on 4173 can otherwise be reused.
     - Never run two Playwright suites at once.
     - Probe scripts go in the scratchpad, run with `NODE_PATH=<repo>/node_modules`.
   - **Algorithm:** re-amortising schedule; interest multiply-first (D-37). Guarantee (D-55): every payment is within 0.01 of the headline except the final one, which is within 0.02.
   - **Limits (D-54):** amount 10 to 10^15; rate 0 to 75%; tenure 1 to 100 years or 1 to 1,200 months.
   - **DOM contract** (spec §8.3.1, D-43/D-48/D-66):
     - summary figures are found with `getByLabel`;
     - charts are a `<figure>` named by its `<figcaption>`, with the SVG `aria-hidden`;
     - D-66 hooks: `[data-hit-area]` (item k of n at (k − 0.5)/n of the width), `[data-segment]`, `[data-series]`;
     - tooltips have `role="tooltip"`.
   - **Freeze tags:** `g3-tests-approved` (authorised later changes: 749144e D-46, 5751988 D-48, 16c8cc8 D-54/55, 04de524 D-59, 95259bc D-61) and `g3b-visuals-tests-approved` (c62d9c2).
   - **Design:** the "Soft ledger" pastel redesign from the bundle in `design/emi-pastel-redesign/` (kept as received; excluded from Prettier and ESLint).
   - **Chart palette** (validated with the dataviz validator script): light principal #6A50D3, interest #C4512E; dark principal #957EEC, interest #D4703C. Balance and loan use the principal colour.

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **docs/spec/decision-log.md:** D-00 to D-69, append-only. The latest:
     - D-65: visuals approved;
     - D-66: test hooks, approved at G3b;
     - D-67: G3b approved, the three copy gaps closed with my suggestions, and the test-designer's readings;
     - D-68: visuals implementation, **Proposed** for the visuals mini-gate;
     - D-69: sticky form, approved request, implementation for review.
     - Still Proposed or open: D-64 (redesign deviations) and RD-3 (forced-colors borders).
   - **docs/user-stories.md:**
     - S-19 moved from Backlog to v1, with AC-19.1 to 19.4;
     - new S-20 (AC-20.1 to 20.6), S-21 (AC-21.1 to 21.3) and S-22 (AC-22.1 to 22.3);
     - 22 stories and 115 ACs; every Status is still "Not implemented".
   - **docs/jobs-to-be-done.md:** exactly four owner-approved edits: J-2 + S-20, J-5 + S-22, J-8 + S-21, and J-9's S-19 no longer "(backlog)".
   - **docs/spec/technical-spec.md:**
     - §1 scope;
     - §3.1.1 summary.ts API and formatPercent;
     - §7 chart and yearly copy (including `yearly.chart.caption` "Interest and principal paid each year.", grouped `{n}`, tooltips with currency);
     - §8.3.1 contract rows;
     - §8.3.2 chart rules;
     - §16.
   - **docs/process/proposal-visuals.md:** the approved visuals proposal.
   - **src/domain/summary.ts** (new):
     ```ts
     export interface YearRow { year: number; months: number; interest: Decimal; principal: Decimal; balance: Decimal }
     const HUNDRED = new Decimal(100)
     const round1 = (x: Decimal) => x.toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)
     export function costSplit(loan: CalculatedLoan) { const interestPercent = round1(loan.totalInterest.times(HUNDRED).div(loan.totalPayable)); return { interestPercent, loanPercent: HUNDRED.minus(interestPercent) } }
     export function interestShare(payment: Decimal, interest: Decimal): Decimal { if (payment.isZero()) return new Decimal(0); return round1(interest.times(HUNDRED).div(payment)) }
     export function yearlySummary(loan): YearRow[]  // groups of 12 rows; exact sums; balance = group's last balance
     ```
   - **src/domain/format.ts:**
     ```ts
     import { Decimal } from './money'
     export function formatPercent(x: Decimal): string { const rounded = x.toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP); return `${rounded.isZero() ? '0.0' : rounded.toFixed(1)}%` }
     ```
   - **src/ui/copy.ts:**
     - `chart.cost` (title, summary(pct), loan, interest);
     - `chart.balance` (title, summary(amount, zero, months, count) with month/months, tooltip(month, balance));
     - `chart.makeup` (title, summary(first, last), tooltip(month, principal, interest));
     - `chart.series` (principal, interest);
     - `yearly` (title, chartCaption, cols(currency), tooltip(year, principal, interest)).
   - **src/ui/components/charts/chartGeometry.ts:**
     - `VIEW_W = 1000` and `VIEW_H = 100`;
     - `ratio(value, max)`: Decimal division, then `toDecimalPlaces(6).toNumber()`; used only for geometry;
     - `stepBandPath(top, bottom?)`: one stepped-area path;
     - `barsPath(top, bottom, fill = 0.64)`;
     - `centrePercent(k, n)`;
     - `useBandHover(count)`: pointermove sets `index = floor(f × count)`;
     - `groupCount(n)`.
   - **src/ui/components/charts/ChartParts.tsx:**
     - `Legend({ first })`: HTML `ul.chart-legend` with swatches;
     - `AxisEnds({ count })`: numbers only, "1" and n;
     - `Tooltip`: `div role="tooltip"` with `left: x%` and `translateX(-x%)`;
     - `HoverBand`: a rect with hard-coded 1000/100 (reviewer F-3).
   - **The four chart components** (in `src/ui/components/charts/`):
     - **CostBreakdown.tsx:** h3 title; `figure.chart` containing `div.cost-bar` with `span[data-segment=loan][data-series=loan]` and, only when the interest is non-zero, `span[data-segment=interest][data-series=interest]` (flexGrow = the percentages); legend; figcaption.
     - **BalanceChart.tsx:** has a duplicate import of `../../../domain/money` (F-3). An SVG `.chart-plot` with `preserveAspectRatio="none"`, `aria-hidden`, `data-hit-area` and the hover handlers, plus `path.mark-principal[data-series=balance]`.
     - **PaymentMakeupChart.tsx:** a principal path plus an interest path stacked on it.
     - **YearlySummary.tsx:** h3 `#yearly-title`; figure with the bars SVG, legend and caption; then `table.yearly-table[aria-labelledby=yearly-title]` with `td` cells (F-3 suggests a `th` row header).
   - **src/ui/components/ResultsPanel.tsx:** after RoundingNote, renders `CostBreakdown`, `BalanceChart`, `PaymentMakeupChart`, `YearlySummary`, then `ScheduleTable`. The stale message uses `className="status status-stale"` (P1).
   - **src/ui/App.tsx:**
     ```tsx
     <main className="layout">
       {/* No semantics: bounds the sticky form to the form/results row (D-69). */}
       <div className="layout-main"><LoanForm /><ResultsPanel /></div>
       <HistoryPanel />
     </main>
     ```
   - **src/ui/theme.css:** the redesign tokens, plus `--chart-principal` and `--chart-interest` in the light, dark and fallback-media blocks.
   - **src/ui/app.css:**
     - the redesign CSS with the D-64 deviations (removed `body overflow-x: hidden`; `.field-error:empty::before { content: none }`; a `.fatal` style);
     - `.layout` is a single column, and `.layout-main` is the 4fr/6fr grid (both single column at ≤ 768 px);
     - the sticky rule:
       ```css
       @media (min-width: 769px) and (min-height: 820px) { .form-card { position: sticky; top: var(--space-6); } }
       ```
     - section 14, charts: `.chart-block`, `figure.chart`, `.chart-plot { height: 140px }`, `.mark-*`, `.chart-hover-band`, `.chart-axis`, `.chart-legend`, `.swatch`, `.chart-tooltip { pointer-events: none }`, `.cost-bar { display: flex; gap: 2px }`, `.cost-segment`, `.yearly-table` (not a scroll region), and a ≤ 560 px media block.
   - **New test files** (frozen at g3b):
     - src/domain/summary.test.ts and src/domain/format-percent.test.ts;
     - e2e/visual-helpers.ts;
     - e2e/s19-yearly.spec.ts, s20-cost.spec.ts, s21-balance-chart.spec.ts and s22-makeup.spec.ts.
   - **Reviewer files:**
     - e2e/review/g45.spec.ts (REVIEW-1/2, passing);
     - **e2e/review/visuals.spec.ts** (new; [REVIEW-V1] and [REVIEW-V2], currently failing);
     - docs/process/review-findings.md (findings sections through "Visuals").
   - **Recent commits:** a5ee7e7 (domain); 0d9967c, fd97fa6, e30a41d, 0f656e4, 323f1f3, 0dc743a (charts); a19ea7f (sticky); 4333476 (D-68/D-69 docs). The branch is `v1`. There is no GitHub remote yet.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **A stale vite preview on port 4173 served an old build:** I stopped it and use `CI=1` for every E2E run (D-49).
   - **Playwright's `--grep` is case-insensitive** and an exclusion filter silently dropped AC-6.1: I now list excluded tests with `--list`.
   - **I labelled an empty probe placeholder as a real "two-tab probe":** I corrected it and ran the real probe.
   - **My Playwright runs collided with the reviewer's** (ENOENT trace files): no concurrent runs from then on.
   - **False "WebKit 3× slower" claim:** an alternating A/B disproved it, and I retracted it in D-64.
   - **Bash heredoc parse failure on a large Python script:** I wrote scripts to scratchpad files instead (d65_docs.py, d67_docs.py, d68_docs.py).
   - **A chain broke because `grep -c` returns exit 1 on a count of 0:** I re-ran the remaining steps.
   - **A `/tmp` script couldn't find `@playwright/test`:** moved to the scratchpad and set NODE_PATH.
   - **TypeScript error on `x.constructor.ROUND_HALF_UP`:** imported `Decimal` from `./money` instead.
   - **The `.field-error:empty` replacement matched twice:** anchored it with a newline.
   - **`mv` of the bundle was denied** (a file was open in the IDE): copied it byte-identically, then removed the original.
   - **Prettier `format:check` failed on the design bundle:** added `design/` to .prettierignore and to ESLint `globalIgnores` (D-62).
   - **The sticky form overlapped Saved calculations:** added the `.layout-main` wrapper, so the sticky containing block ends at the results.
   - **Flaky AC-8.4** (Chromium smooth-scroll race): an owner-approved test fix, D-61.
   - **Firefox-only AC-8.1 tab-past-the-end quirk:** an owner-approved portable assertion, D-59.
   - **Recurring WebKit 8 s or 30 s click timeouts under full-suite load:** they pass in isolation, and verify passed on re-runs. The latest reviewer run had 2 §9.3 two-tab WebKit failures (F-4), which passed 40/40 on later runs and with one worker.

5. Problem Solving:
   - **Visuals:** implemented and committed. Verify passed with 543/543 E2E on my runs (the second and the post-sticky runs).
   - **Reviewer's latest findings** (BLOCKING 0):
     - **F-1 Major:** at 180 px (200% zoom) after L-B or L-MAX, the page scrolls sideways by 129 px, because `table.yearly-table` can't shrink. [REVIEW-V1] is red in all 3 browsers.
     - **F-2 Major** (the open RD-3): in forced-colors mode in Chromium and Firefox, the cost-bar segments and legend swatches become Canvas with no border, so they're invisible. [REVIEW-V2] is red in Chromium and Firefox.
     - **F-3 Minor:**
       - unused `copy.chart.cost.interest` (the legend uses `copy.chart.series.interest`);
       - duplicate money import in BalanceChart;
       - HoverBand hard-codes 1000/100;
       - the Year column is a `td`, not a row header.
     - **F-4 Minor:** WebKit §9.3 two-tab load flake, seen only at HEAD.
     - **F-5 Minor:** the hover index isn't reset when the loan changes; not reproducible.
     - The reviewer also suggested making "ratio and percentages may be JS numbers for geometry" an explicit carve-out in the spec.

6. All user messages:
   - "Can you go through the whole folder and share your thoughts?"
   - "1- should be fixed, 2- we will do at end"
   - "what questions do you have for me right now?"
   - The list answering items 1 to 13: CLAUDE.md formatting yes; this is the planning phase; keep 2 dp; keep AC-12.6 and add a dialog line; reword AC-8.5; items 6 to 12 approved; "Let's create a repo then." Also: "Right you are going to come up with solid plan, You will implement everything in phases story by story."
